        "Rural female LFPR is 50.0% among women with below-10th education, falls to 33.0% for those with education between Class 10 and a diploma, then recovers to 45.8% among graduates. The urban pattern has the same shape at a lower level: 27.3%, 18.7%, and 39.8%.",
        "<b>Udaiti's Take —</b> The blue-collar workforce in large enterprises stood at nearly 6 million in 2024–25, and has been growing rapidly, at 17% CAGR since 2022–23 (BRSR filings of listed NSE firms). Partnerships between state governments and employers can improve women's access to entry-level formal roles by building awareness and aspiration and removing demand-side and ecosystem barriers."
