        "<b>Udaiti's Take —</b> Casual labour is where India's gender and rural crises intersect. The 20.9 million women in agricultural casual labour are the least protected and most invisible in policy discourse. Collective organising, legal literacy, and wage transparency can meaningfully improve conditions for this group."
