        "Across the 12 sub-sectors tracked, women's share of the workforce ranges from 4% (fabricated metals) to 28% (apparel). The fastest-growing sub-sectors — Auto and Chemicals, both at 20% CAGR since 2022 — are among the sectors where women are least represented today, at 9% and 15% respectively.",
        "<b>Udaiti's Take —</b> Formal job growth in manufacturing is concentrated in a handful of high-density sub-sectors. Clusters co-locate demand, supply, and infrastructure, which increases potential impact and reduces the cost of intervention. The effectiveness of any programme, however, depends on two things: the state's willingness to work with nonprofits, and the baseline infrastructure already in place for women workers."
